 "text": "Hey, how's your day been so far? Not necessarily, it depends on the style. Would you call it cheating if you used a photo reference for a still life painting? That's bit petty, and different people do it differently. Some artists trace or work from photos all the time. Probably faster and freer, because you can zoom in on the details and fix mistakes. It is. I'd suggest drawing from life as much as possible though. That really improves hand-eye coordination.",
